From cc2b18de270e77b8921b7ceaef76f0c64b287b04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:34:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(copy-drafts): kill verification rows past the device's
 draft limits

Base: candidate-37's patch head 5b7cfa37f (tree af0fb152), the series of
experiments/2026-10-26-spark-ds41f-candidate/candidate-37/vllm/series. The
alternative to 8bb508091 (#856), which makes the host wait for the limit copy.

Rationale (#852): patch 0612 made CopyDrafter.sync_slot_draft_limits publish
the host's per-slot draft limits only once their copy has landed, so the
adaptive budget can read an older proposal's limits. A stale limit wider than
the current proposal lets the step verify rows the proposal does not have, its
-1 placeholders. With dead rows off (SPARK_DS41F_DSPARK_DEAD_ROWS_TAU unset or
0) they are routed live, and route_partials asserts on non-finite gate logits.

The device's limits (slot_draft_limits.gpu) are always the current proposal's:
copy_alloc writes them before the drafter runs, on the stream every later
step's input preparation runs on. The draft combine now takes them
(DeadRows.limits) whenever copy drafts are on, with or without dead rows:
- a decoding request's cut is at most its slot's limit (the survival cut
  clamped to it, or without dead rows its drafts up to it, a thread a request
  as the plain combine);
- the rows from the cut on are padding, which route_partials and the MoE
  dispatch skip;
- a row past the limit takes the request's last sampled token as its input id
  instead of -1.
The cut then clamps what the request commits (the token counts, block
verification's end of block, the acceptance estimator's observations), so no
row past the limit is ever accepted. The runner declares the cut and combine
variants with copy drafts. The host keeps 0612's non-blocking read: nothing
waits.

Design: Jordi Posthumus (#852, #855) found the cause, measured it (stale-limit
reads, the -1 -> 0 control) and proposed the device-side clamp this change
completes (#855, c30d6b6): the device limits rather than the host's decide,
the rows past them are dead, and they take the request's last sampled token
as their input id. This version also clamps without dead rows, where those
rows were routed live. It clamps the cut to the limit instead of zeroing the
confidences past it (copy_select already writes 0 there). It rewrites only the
ids past the limit, so rows dead by survival within a proposal keep their
bits.

Quality: where the host's limits are current no row is past the device limit,
and every step's input ids, padding, logits rows and commit counts are the same
bits (the cut equals the request's drafts, so no clamp binds). Where they are
stale and wider, the extra rows are padding and the request commits at most
the proposal's drafts and the bonus; temperature-0 text is unchanged. Where
they are stale and narrower, drafts are still left out: the device can only
remove rows the host scheduled (#856's wait fixes that; this does not). Copy
drafts with block verification on its Triton kernels (FP64 draws, a watermark)
are now refused at kernel declaration, as dead rows are: those kernels cannot
end a block at a cut. Given the same layout every rank marks the same rows:
the device limits are computed alike on every rank from the same histories and
verification. The layout itself still comes from each rank's own host read,
which this change does not touch.

Tests:
- tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_tilelang_inputs.py: the draft limits against a host
  reference, with and without dead rows; limits no request reaches change
  nothing; the declared combine variants are the launched ones.
- tests/v1/spec_decode/test_copy_drafts.py, through a CopyDrafter and the
  adaptive verification manager: a stale wider host limit routes no
  placeholder row, with dead rows off and on (on the unpatched code, with the
  limits handed to the manager, its rows past the limit keep -1 ids and, with
  dead rows off, stay live: the test fails there); current host limits leave
  the step bit for bit as before; a stale narrower limit still under-admits.
  0612's test that sync_slot_draft_limits never blocks is kept.
- tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py: dead_row_args carries
  the device limits.
- tests/v1/worker/test_prepare_kernels.py: the cut and combine variants are
  declared with copy drafts and dead rows off.

Upstream status: local (spark-ds41f). Copy drafts, adaptive verification's
dead rows and the TileLang input kernels are local patches.
